<?php
/**
 * Spartrak Header Account Chip.
 *
 * FIGMA SSOT: node 595:14513 ("Profile") — a 40px-tall pill, 1px
 * border/default on bg/surface, padding-inline start 14 / end 6, 8px gaps,
 * children in RTL order [avatar 28px, first name 14px Medium, chevron 16px].
 * Geometry verified by measurement on the 1440 export (chip 144..264, chevron
 * box 150..166, name 175..213, avatar plate 222..250).
 *
 * Replaces the bare `header.links` list the previous header rendered in this
 * slot. Until 2026-08-27 that block was re-declared as this chip's child so
 * Magento's own account links rendered inside the dropdown; it now renders the
 * account navigation Figma specifies instead — see "THE SIGNED-IN MENU" below
 * for what those core links were doing wrong and why state-independent routes
 * are the fix rather than a workaround.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * SERVER-SIDE IS THE FIRST PAINT; customerData IS THE AUTHORITY
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * QA FIX (2026-08-27) — reported symptom: the desktop chip intermittently
 * showed "تسجيل الدخول" (sign in) to a signed-in shopper, while the MOBILE
 * drawer on the very same page load showed that shopper's real name. That
 * combination is the diagnosis: within one response, customerData knew the
 * visitor was signed in and the server-rendered HTML did not.
 *
 * HISTORY. The 2026-08-25 pass moved the decision from customerData into PHP,
 * reading Magento\Framework\App\Http\Context via
 * Spartrak\CustomerAuth\ViewModel\CustomerState, on the reasoning that
 * HttpContext is the object Magento's own full-page cache varies on and is
 * therefore safe to branch on inside a cached page. That reasoning is correct
 * ABOUT MAGENTO'S FPC — and insufficient here, because Magento's FPC is not
 * the only cache in front of this store. The live responses carry an
 * `x-cache-nxaccel` header: there is a separate HTTP cache layer ahead of
 * Magento whose key we neither control nor can see from the theme. Any layer
 * that serves one visitor's HTML to another turns a PHP branch on session
 * state into exactly the bug reported, and no amount of correctness inside
 * Magento can fix a variant chosen upstream of it.
 *
 * So the STATE decision is client-side again — but this version is not a
 * repeat of the pre-2026-08-25 build, which failed for an unrelated and
 * since-fixed reason (sections.xml keyed its actions on the route id instead
 * of the URL path, so signing in invalidated nothing and the `customer`
 * section was never fetched at all). Two things are different now:
 *
 *   1. THE SECTION ACTUALLY RESOLVES. That sections.xml bug is fixed, and the
 *      mobile drawer — which has used this exact contract throughout — is the
 *      standing proof: it reports the right name on the same page loads where
 *      this chip reported the wrong state.
 *
 *   2. PHP STILL CHOOSES THE FIRST PAINT. CustomerState has not been removed;
 *      it now sets which of the two chips starts un-`hidden`. On a correctly
 *      keyed response that guess is right, so there is no flash, no toggle and
 *      no layout shift — the same rendering the server-side-only version gave.
 *      When the guess is wrong, the widget corrects it instead of leaving a
 *      shopper greeted as a stranger. A server-side HINT is safe where a
 *      server-side VERDICT is not.
 *
 * This is also what Magento core itself does for this element: the Luma header
 * ships Magento_Customer/js/view/authentication-link, a customerData-driven
 * component, in preference to the HttpContext-driven
 * Customer\Block\Account\AuthorizationLink.
 *
 * The NAME was always client-side and stays that way: a customer's name is not
 * a cache-vary dimension, and making it one would give every shopper a private
 * copy of every page.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * TWO DELIBERATE DEPARTURES FROM THE FRAME — both flagged in the handover
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * 1. NO AVATAR PHOTOGRAPH. Figma fills the 28px circle with a stock
 *    head-and-shoulders photo (the same raster the logo is cropped out of).
 *    Magento has no customer-avatar feature, so shipping it would render one
 *    stock person's face as EVERY signed-in shopper's avatar. It is a design
 *    placeholder, not a brand asset. The plate's size, radius and colour
 *    (blue/0 #f4f7fd) are reproduced exactly and filled with the customer's
 *    own initial — real data, nothing invented, no asset authored.
 *
 * 2. THE GUEST STATE IS NOT IN FIGMA. Every header frame in the file shows the
 *    signed-in chip; no frame shows what a first-time visitor sees, which is
 *    what most visitors see. Implemented as the same pill with a sign-in label
 *    and no avatar plate (there is no initial to put in it), opening the
 *    existing auth modal. Geometry, tokens and type are the signed-in chip's;
 *    only the contents differ. Needs a designer decision, not a guess.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 */
$customerState = $block->getData('customer_state');

// The FIRST-PAINT guess only — see the header note. spartrak-utility-header.js
// overrides it from the customerData `customer` section once that resolves.
$isLoggedIn = $customerState !== null && $customerState->isLoggedIn();
?>
<div class="spartrak-header__account-guest" data-account-guest<?= $isLoggedIn ? ' hidden' : '' ?>>
    <button
        type="button"
        class="spartrak-header__account-chip"
        data-auth-open
    >
        <span class="spartrak-header__account-name"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Sign in')) ?></span>
        <span class="spartrak-header__account-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </button>
</div>

<div class="spartrak-header__account-customer" data-account-customer<?= $isLoggedIn ? '' : ' hidden' ?>>
    <button
        type="button"
        class="spartrak-header__account-chip"
        data-account-toggle
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="spartrak-account-menu"
    >
        <?php /* Node 693:45429. The initial and the name are written by the
                 widget from the customerData `customer` section. The name
                 falls back to a neutral label rather than a guessed one, and
                 the initial starts EMPTY so the plate can never flash the
                 wrong letter before the section resolves. */ ?>
        <span class="spartrak-header__avatar" aria-hidden="true" data-account-initial></span>
        <span class="spartrak-header__account-name" data-account-name><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('My account')) ?></span>
        <span class="spartrak-header__account-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </button>

    <?php
    /**
     * ======================================================================
     * THE SIGNED-IN MENU — REBUILT FROM FIGMA 2026-08-27
     * ======================================================================
     * FIGMA SSOT: node 562:11000 ("Sidebar") on the My Account page — its
     * "Menu Container" (562:11002) is the design system's account-navigation
     * pattern, and this dropdown is now an instance of it rather than an
     * un-designed list. Rows are 48px, `px-12 py-8`, gap 12, label
     * Body/Small Medium (14px/500) in text/secondary with a 20px icon at the
     * inline end, 8px between rows; the active row takes bg/field with its
     * label in text/primary; sign-out is separated and rendered in
     * text/price-sale. Every one of those values is read from that node.
     *
     * WHY IT NO LONGER RENDERS `header.links`.
     * It used to emit Magento's own header-links block, and on the live site
     * that produced "Compare (0 items) / Sign In / تواصل معنا / Create an
     * Account" INSIDE the menu of a shopper who was already signed in. Two
     * separate faults:
     *
     *   1. WRONG STATE. Magento\Customer\Block\Account\AuthorizationLink and
     *      RegisterLink decide guest-vs-signed-in from HttpContext — the same
     *      server-side branch that the chip itself had to stop trusting (see
     *      the note at the top of this file). Cached upstream, they render the
     *      guest pair to a signed-in shopper. Offering "Sign In" and "Create
     *      an Account" inside the account menu is the visible symptom.
     *
     *   2. WRONG CONTENT. This menu is only reachable FROM the signed-in chip
     *      — a guest gets the auth modal instead — so guest links are
     *      unreachable-by-design, and a compare-list link is not account
     *      navigation at all.
     *
     * The links below are all STATE-INDEPENDENT routes: they are the same URL
     * for every visitor, so nothing here can be wrong in a cached page. That
     * is the property that makes this menu immune to the bug above, not just
     * patched against it.
     *
     * The block declaration was removed from Smartwave_Porto/layout/default.xml
     * in the same change, so no block is left rendered-but-unused.
     *
     * NOT IMPLEMENTED, DELIBERATELY: Figma draws a count badge on "طلباتي"
     * (node 562:11010). Magento ships no order-count customer-data section, and
     * CLAUDE.md §5/§9 forbid inventing or hardcoding the number, so the badge
     * is omitted rather than faked. It needs a real section to exist first.
     */
    $accountLinks = [
        ['route' => 'customer/account',    'label' => __('My account'),      'icon' => 'account-user.svg',      'mod' => 'user'],
        ['route' => 'sales/order/history', 'label' => __('My orders'),       'icon' => 'account-orders.svg',    'mod' => 'orders'],
        ['route' => 'customer/address',    'label' => __('My addresses'),    'icon' => 'account-addresses.svg', 'mod' => 'addresses'],
        ['route' => 'wishlist',            'label' => __('My wishlist'),     'icon' => 'heart.svg',             'mod' => 'wishlist'],
        ['route' => 'contact',             'label' => __('Help and support'),'icon' => 'account-support.svg',   'mod' => 'support'],
    ];
    ?>
    <div class="spartrak-header__account-menu" id="spartrak-account-menu" hidden>
        <ul class="spartrak-header__account-links">
            <?php foreach ($accountLinks as $link) : ?>
                <li>
                    <a class="spartrak-header__account-link" href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($block->getUrl($link['route'])) ?>">
                        <span class="spartrak-header__account-link-label"><?= $block->escapeHtml($link['label']) ?></span>
                        <span class="spartrak-header__account-link-icon spartrak-header__account-link-icon--<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($link['mod']) ?>" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    </a>
                </li>
            <?php endforeach; ?>
        </ul>

        <?php /* Node 562:11021 — pinned below the list, its own group, and the
                 only row that is not text/secondary. A plain GET link:
                 Magento\Customer\Controller\Account\Logout implements
                 HttpGetActionInterface (as well as POST), which is exactly how
                 core's own AuthorizationLink renders it. */ ?>
        <a class="spartrak-header__account-link spartrak-header__account-link--signout"
           href="<?= $block->escapeUrl($block->getUrl('customer/account/logout')) ?>">
            <span class="spartrak-header__account-link-label"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Sign out')) ?></span>
            <span class="spartrak-header__account-link-icon spartrak-header__account-link-icon--signout" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>
